 "comment": "OWNER OF MATH-MODE COMMANDS. Control words that content and definition bodies may use inside mathematics without a registry entry: amsmath layout, relations, bound-variable Greek letters, accents, and the structural macros of latex/tpc-macros.sty. Greek letters and glyphs that the registry owns (\\mu, \\rho, \\Delta, \\Omega, \\sigma, ...) are deliberately absent: content must use the semantic macro. This file does NOT list text-mode constructs: sectioning, environments, text macros (\\emph, \\ref, \\claim, \\tpcdef, ...), the switch \\text and the forbidden list (\\input, \\cite, \\includegraphics, \\tag, ...) are owned by docs/authoring/contract.json and enforced by scripts/course/check_levels.py. check_registry.py reads the contract's text macros from there and fails ('allow-list conflict') on any word listed here that the contract owns or forbids. allowed_prefixes is empty for the same reason: a prefix would admit \\tpcsetchapter and \\tpcdeclaredef, which the contract forbids in content.",
